---
import BaseLayout from '../shared/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Prompt from '../shared/ui/Prompt.astro';
import { profile } from '../features/seo/seo';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Privacy Policy | ${profile.contact.name}`} description="What amrithnath.dev does and does not collect: no cookies, forms or tracking, plus how analytics, view counts and the carbon badge work." currentPage="/privacy-policy">
  <Prompt command="cat privacy-policy.md" />
  <div class="output">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 28 Oct 2026</p>

      <p>I'm {profile.contact.name}, and amrithnath.dev is my personal website. This policy explains what happens to information about you when you visit it. In short: I don't run accounts, contact forms, newsletters or messaging services, I don't set cookies, and I don't sell or share anything about you.</p>

      <h2>What I Collect</h2>
      <p>I don't ask you for any personal information, and the site has no forms that send me data. The site search runs in your browser.</p>
      <p>If you email me using one of the links on the site, your own email app sends the message, and I receive your email address and whatever you write. I use it only to reply, and I don't add you to any list.</p>
      <p>Like any website, the hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes your IP address and standard request details to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. I use this only in aggregate (see analytics below) and don't use it to identify you.</p>

      <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>
      <p>I don't sell, trade, or rent your information. The only other parties involved are the services described below that make the site work, and I'd disclose information only if the law required it.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
      <p>This website does not set cookies. It stores your theme preference in your browser's local storage, which never leaves your device.</p>
      <p>Page views are counted with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which is cookieless and does not fingerprint or track you across sites. It records aggregate data only: the page visited, referrer, country, and browser and device type. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, the analytics script is not loaded at all. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

      <p>Site search runs in your browser using a same-origin, build-time index. The search page does not load analytics or send queries to an external search service. Shared search URLs include the query, so it may appear in browser history and site access logs.</p>
      <h3>Privacy check</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/privacy-check/">privacy check</a> page shows what any website can learn about your browser. To demonstrate fingerprinting it reads your browser's characteristics, but the results are only displayed on that page: they are never sent anywhere or stored, and are discarded when you leave. That page loads no analytics, and its carbon estimate is calculated locally. When you run the check, your browser requests an empty bait file from this site to detect content blockers and, unless you add <code>--offline</code>, downloads the public Chrome or Firefox release list from <a href="https://endoflife.date/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">endoflife.date</a> without cookies or a referrer; your version number is not sent. Only if you add <code>--stun</code> does your browser contact Cloudflare's public STUN server, which sees your IP address in order to report it back to you.</p>
      <h3>Article view counts</h3>
      <p>Blog posts and project pages may show a public view count. It is a single anonymous number per page, kept by a small service at <code>views.amrithnath.dev</code> on Cloudflare. When you open an article, your browser asks that service for the count and, the first time you view that article, adds one to it. The service stores only the page path and its total. It does not set cookies and does not store your IP address, browser details, or any identifier, so views cannot be linked to you or to each other.</p>
      <p>To avoid counting you twice, your browser remembers in local storage which articles it has already counted; this never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, the count is only displayed and never increased.</p>

      <h3>Carbon badge</h3>
      <p>The footer shows an estimate of the page's carbon footprint. On this site, your browser asks the Website Carbon API (<code>api.websitecarbon.com</code>, run by Wholegrain Digital) for the result for the page address you are viewing, without cookies or a referrer, and caches the answer in local storage for a day. As with any web request, that service receives your IP address. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, no request is made; in that case, or if the service is unavailable, the estimate is calculated entirely in your browser from the page's own size.</p>
      <p>On wide screens the side panel also shows live page performance and a carbon estimate calculated in your browser; that data never leaves your device apart from a running byte total kept in session storage.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>The website may contain links to third-party sites. I'm not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites, so check their policies before sharing personal information with them.</p>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>The site is served only over HTTPS with a strict Content Security Policy and other security headers. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, so I can't guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>If you've emailed me, you can ask me to show, correct, or delete what I hold about you. Since the site itself keeps no personal data, there is nothing else to request. Contact <a href="mailto:amrithnathvijayakumar@gmail.com">amrithnathvijayakumar@gmail.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>I may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
